<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran denies role in fridge hack, France summons ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f0b7157961f9df8738e6877693f6503b7e5d33f05517283a88e4a751ff8bb8d</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206--6d0355211a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France has said it rules "nothing" out in response to a cyberattack on supermarket refrigeration units. Iran, however, said it categorically rejected Paris' "baseless and one-sided accusations" of IRGC involvement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d66706e0d7992fcce95d329aea1ba4df6cab038eee8276591c68865ac78cf405</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Krakow shooting suspect 'fascinated' by Norwegian mass murder Anders Breivik, says justice minister</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:283f719bf222540d542da8f09237570ddf1b296f857f61a360331cb77df3c138</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-krakow-shooting-suspect-fascinated-by-norwegian-mass-murder-anders-breivik-says-justice-minis/a-79910435--6c31a3e79cc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-krakow-shooting-suspect-fascinated-by-norwegian-mass-murder-anders-breivik-says-justice-minister/a-79910435?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 24-year old suspect was found to have read a significant amount of material about Breivik and other far-right figures. Speculation over his motives have prompted a bitter political feud in Warsaw.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2d0c9f8e91c82f05c41727cca88ac17cd93e15fcbd9b47da049ec7b1d9a31d3</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:661f9ffb42e3cda65c6cccb39ccc938e8a773c78a09ecfaf6d367255263f1bbc</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo vs. Javier Milei: How political is the pope?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a78834c8fdbe06d98ef286c94da3f61c3da46e9e9682682d1e20a3495e32f91f</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-vs-javier-milei-how-political-is-the-pope/a-79907666--31a87b963c2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-vs-javier-milei-how-political-is-the-pope/a-79907666?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV's tour of South America has drawn huge crowds — and a measure of political controversy. Perceived criticism of Argentina's leader, and earlier rebukes of Donald Trump, offer a glimpse into papacy politics.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Japan watches for signs of change in Trump's foreign policy priorities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8e6ecc969759c06eff7afe98c64c8e65f9a45cf79ed848c8804a3f8fa261dd9</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" hr